    "interpretation": "The verified NoiseALU.mul() ALREADY uses shift-add (bit operations). Multiplication is implemented as: while b>0: if b&1: result+=a; a<<=1; b>>=1. This IS native bit-ops multiplication \u2014 no Python int multiplication is used in the actual computation (only the shift-add loop)."
